  "body": "## Cause\n\nCommit `ac03087a3` (PR #3684) changed where a tabbed outside 2D Contour starts its untabbed levels. Now an untabbed level that is alone on its level starts at the same point as the tabbed level. The committed demo `examples/first-router-part.camproj` kept the old cached path of `2D Contour1`. The test `first_router_part_project_loads_verifies_and_posts_to_grblhal` rebuilds the demo by commands. It compares the two posted programs and failed at `crates/app/tests/first_router_part.rs:282`. The contour stamp did not change, so the old cache read as fresh.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe demo was regenerated by the documented commands only. There is no hand edit.\n\n1. `WRITE_GOLDEN=1 cargo test -p camcraft-app --test first_router_part` writes `examples/first-router-part.camproj`.\n2. `camcraft-cli process examples/first-router-part.camproj -o examples/first-router-part.nc` writes the program.\n\n## Readings\n\n`examples/first-router-part.nc`: only the `2D Contour1` section changes (lines 81-132, section header at line 78).\n\n- The line count stays at 165.\n- The depths (Z-4, Z-8, Z-9 and the tab level Z-12) do not change.\n- The feeds (F400 plunge, F1800 cut), S9500, and the Z15 and Z2 heights do not change.\n- Old start of the untabbed levels Z-4, Z-8, Z-9: X173.514 Y24.198, with an arc lead into the corner at X170 Y27. Old exit: X167.711 Y23.694.\n- New start of the same levels: X176 Y80.991, with an arc lead onto the right side at X173 Y77.991. New exit: X176 Y74.991.\n- The new start is the start of the tabbed level Z-12. The Z-12 level does not change.\n- The drill and pocket sections do not change.\n\n`examples/first-router-part.camproj`: the writer made these changes outside the contour cache.\n\n- `\"version\": 73` becomes `78`. This is the current file version of the writer.\n- In the stored machine block, `\"kind\": \"mill\"` becomes `\"router\"`. The source is the machine file `assets/machines/sienci-altmill-4x4.mch`, changed by `afa612d2f`.\n- In the stored machine block, `\"post\": \"grblHAL\"` is new. The source is the same machine file, changed by `2fdc4200f`.\n\nAll other changes are in the cached moves of `2D Contour1`. No operation parameter changes. No stamp changes. The `2D Pocket1` and `Drill1` caches do not change. The posted program changes only in `2D Contour1`.\n\n## Tests (quick gate, debug, on the final head)\n\n- `camcraft-app --test first_router_part`: 4 passed. It was red before: 3 passed, 1 failed at line 282.\n- `camcraft-app --test first_part_programs`: 2 passed. This test pins the `.nc`.\n- `camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: 39 passed, 4 ignored.\n- `camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting`: 2 passed.\n- `camcraft-motion --test contour_tab_entry`: 3 passed. This test pins #3684.\n\nThe guide pages that name the demo quote no changed contour line or number. No guide file changes.\n\n## Not changed / not exercised\n\n- The op stamp salt (`crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs:46`) is not changed. The comment at that line asks for a bump only when a verify law that a cache records changes. No written rule asks for a bump when generator output changes. Thus a project saved before #3684 posts the old contour start until the user regenerates the operation.\n- Heavy lanes and the light lane were not run. This is a `P2` PR with no code change.\n- The GUI was not opened.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #3698\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
